ifa/issues/124 -- a comprehension used as a list INDEX leaves the indexed list element type untyped (_CG_void), so codegen must guess a layout for it. Reduced from shedskin_examples/go 635 -> 10 lines; the same imprecision is what lets ifa/123 pick the wrong layout and corrupt a field. Runs with --refuse-imprecise so the test asserts the CORRECT behaviour -- compiles clean and prints 2 -- and flips to PASS by itself when inference resolves the element type.
